   must-reject fixtures (incl. operational content under defensive framing / in think traces),
   explicit precedence (operational content dominates), ambiguous-case handling, and acceptance
   gating before scoring.
4. **Major — §8.2 fixture not transcribed into the plan.** FIXED: the verbatim 578-char reply
   is embedded in §8.2 (fixture path also given); the stored-reply test and the fresh-response
   test are separate requirements.
5. **Major — refusal-vocabulary defect unresolved; recall vs generalization conflated.**
   FIXED: §8.4 uses the fixed expanded refusal vocabulary independent of leak detection;
   outcomes (REFUSED / ANSWERED-DEFENSIVELY / MIXED) defined; 1,100 battery identified as
   retention/recall with frozen method (Newcombe paired 95% CI, conservative missing policy,
   strict > −0.10); fresh 200-probe generalization set measured with the same bound.
6. **Major — §8.6 mixed sample support with metric tolerance.** FIXED: explicit margins
   (loss Δ ≤ 0.0, token-F1 Δ ≥ −0.02 — v2's margins, unchanged), pooled + per-dataset rule,
   min support 610, missing-output handling (>5% missing invalidates).
7. **Major — §8.5 carried the merge lesson only partially.** FIXED: bounded claim with bf16
   reference arithmetic, non-finite rejection, near-zero absolute bound; the old
   zero-first-position-disagreement requirement explicitly excluded from this gate; no claim
   of whole-model behavioral equivalence.
8. **Major — STRONG branch not an available mixture.** FIXED: §4 distinguishes specified vs
   available; the no-trail build is the default and the only approvable mixture until the
   quality verdict + gate receipts land; STRONG selection needs a second approval.
9. **Major — stop condition not reproducible; §7 conjunction could reject valid updates.**
   FIXED: §5.2 defines the rule on logged observations (every 10 optimizer steps, 6
   consecutive = 60 steps, baseline = first 30 post-warmup observations); §7 uses weight-hash
