### Pass-3 review (2026-09-29): REJECT, 5 Major + 1 Minor findings — rev 4 claimed resolution, but the pass-4 audit (below) showed items 1 (F1 conservatism) and 2 (G-A2 exclusion instruction) were NOT resolved; superseded by the pass-4 section. Entries otherwise preserved unchanged.

Review: gpt-6-astra, codex 0.155.1, read-only sandbox, 2026-09-29; verdict REJECT; output
`research-tmp/reviews/plan-v3-pass3-output.txt`. The pass-1 and pass-2 disposition tables above are
preserved unchanged; each pass-3 finding is addressed below (§ references are to this revision).

1. **Major — held-out missing-value handling could turn a genuine failure into PASS.** FIXED: §8.6
   now requires complete reference-loss measurement (cross-entropy loss is unbounded above — no
   defensible finite imputation exists; any missing loss row invalidates the loss component →
   NO-SHIP, re-run to completion). F1 uses asymmetric imputation on the bounded [0,1] scale:
   tuned-missing → 0; base-missing → that dataset's maximum observed base F1, which can only lower
   Δ and never inflate it [rev-4 claim — REJECTED by pass-4 finding 1: the observed-max imputation
   can flip a genuine FAIL to PASS; corrected in rev 5 (missing base F1 → actual upper bound 1) —
   see the pass-4 disposition item 1 below]. Symmetric zero-imputation is explicitly rejected. Fixed denominators
   retained; the ≤5% missing-rate floor applies to F1/output missing, pooled AND per-dataset.
2. **Major — fixed evaluation populations conflicted with overlap exclusions.** FIXED: §8.4 (fresh
   200) and §8.8 (G-A2 60) now state the overlap contract explicitly [rev-4 claim for G-A2 —
   REJECTED by pass-4 finding 2: the exclusion instruction survived at §8.8; it is DELETED in rev 5 —
   see the pass-4 disposition item 2 below] — fixed pinned population,
   disjointness re-verified BEFORE scoring, ANY overlap invalidates the instrument → measurement
   missing → NO-SHIP. No replacement, no exclusion, no reduced-n measurement, never treated as
   missing responses. §8.4 also records the scope limitation: the fresh 200 are all
