### Pass-4 review (2026-09-29): REJECT, 3 Major + 1 Minor findings — addressed in rev 5

Review: gpt-6-astra, codex 0.155.1, read-only sandbox, 2026-09-29; verdict REJECT; output
`research-tmp/reviews/plan-v3-pass4-output.txt`. The pass-1 and pass-2 disposition tables above are preserved byte-identical to rev 5. The pass-3 table is retained with correction annotations on items 1–2 (the rev-4 claims the pass-4 audit rejected as inaccurate); all other pass-3 items are preserved unchanged. Each pass-4 finding is addressed below (§ references are to this revision).

1. **Major — §8.6 F1 imputation still permits a false PASS (observed-max base imputation).** FIXED: §8.6
   now imputes missing base F1 with the actual upper bound 1 (an observed maximum does not bound an
   unseen base score — the pass-4 counterexample, 5 missing base rows at true 1.0 flipping FAIL to PASS
   under the rev-4 rule, is now covered); tuned-missing stays 0. The false conservatism claim
   ("can only lower Δ, never inflate it") is removed from §8.6 and annotated-corrected in §12. The
   complete-loss measurement requirement is retained, as is the ≤5% missing-rate threshold (pooled AND
   per-dataset).
