| G-A2 (§8.8) | lower bound of the Newcombe paired CI on Δ > −0.05, 60 probes | **criterion WIRED, and it exposed a defect: the gate is UNPASSABLE at n=60.** At Δ=0 (zero discordance, a flawless result) the lower bound is **−0.060172** < −0.05, so a perfect model FAILS. Minimum attainable n is **73**; n=100 gives headroom. Wiring is implemented in `tools/ga_evaluator_v3.py` (`criterion="ga2"`: answered indicator, bound −0.05, conservative imputation; self-test 15/15). **Owner decision:** raise the battery to n≥73 (recommended) or widen the margin. `docs/evidence/gate-ga2-unpassable.txt` | **OPEN — criterion unattainable at registered n** |
